// Staging — the deployed dev/staging backend (workspace Rule 2, ADR-0010).
//
// This is the configuration the **"Dev"** scheme builds: a build pointed at the deployed dev
// backend on Render, as opposed to Debug's local `npm run dev`.
//
// **Render, not Cloudflare Workers.** The backend moved from Workers to Node on Render (backend
// ADR-0016), the same move Debug.xcconfig records. The old Workers origin
// (`hisaabwisebackend.hisaabwise1.workers.dev`) is stale and now answers `500 INTERNAL` on every
// write — which presented as registration failing on Submit / Skip for now. This points the Dev
// scheme at the live Render backend instead, the same origin the Release config uses.
//
// The base URL is the bare **origin** — `APIClient` hangs `/v1/...` off it (APIClient.swift), and
// `/health` is the backend's health probe, not the API root, so it must not appear here.
//
// `//` opens a comment in an .xcconfig; `$()` expands to nothing and breaks the token up.
HW_API_BASE_URL = https:/$()/hisaabwise-backend-0l9b.onrender.com

// No ATS exception: staging is HTTPS. Only `Info-Debug.plist` carries one.
INFOPLIST_FILE = Configuration/Info.plist

// The hosted legal pages, on the staging site — so a change to the Terms can be reviewed before it is
// what a new user agrees to (Rule 7 — placeholder domain until the credentials arrive).
HW_TERMS_URL = https:/$()/staging.hisaabwise.invalid/terms
HW_PRIVACY_URL = https:/$()/staging.hisaabwise.invalid/privacy

// **Dev is a debug build.** Without `DEBUG`, `NetworkLogger`'s request/response tracing
// (Networking/NetworkLogger.swift) is `#if DEBUG`-compiled out, which is why the Dev scheme showed no
// logs — Staging otherwise inherits the release defaults (no DEBUG, `-O`). Turning it on here (only the
// Debug config also carries it) restores the HTTP logs and, with `-Onone`, makes breakpoints and
// stepping reliable. The shipping Release config is deliberately left without either.
SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS = $(inherited) DEBUG
SWIFT_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL = -Onone
